  <div class="section-header">
    <h2>About</h2>
  </div>

  <div style="max-width: 680px;">

    <p>
      I'm a youth pastor at <strong>Crosspoint Church</strong> in McKinney, TX, where I've been on staff since January 2025.
      I preach on Wednesdays and Sundays to middle and high school students, coordinate volunteers, and oversee small group programming.
    </p>

    <p>
      I'm also pursuing a <strong>Master of Theological Studies (MTS)</strong> at Midwestern Baptist Theological Seminary in Kansas City,
      studying online. I'm currently in my second semester.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem;">Ministry Philosophy</h2>

    <p>
      My mission is to develop resilient believers who love and live for Jesus — students who carry their faith through high school
      and into adulthood, not just teenagers who attend a youth group.
    </p>

    <p>
      I believe the window of youth ministry is irreplaceable. What students encounter — and decide — about Jesus during these years
      shapes the trajectory of their lives. That conviction shapes everything about how I approach teaching, small groups, and pastoral care.
    </p>

    <div class="mission-box" style="margin: 1.5rem 0;">
      "To develop resilient believers who love and live for Jesus by leveraging every advance of our generation
      to point young hearts to the one true Life-Changer: Scripture fulfilled in Christ's cross and resurrection."
    </div>

    <h2 style="margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem;">Teaching Approach</h2>

    <p>
      I preach from an outline rather than a manuscript — prioritizing eye contact, movement, and connection over a polished script.
      My goal is to remove every distraction and confusion from the presentation so the Word of God reaches students' hearts with maximum clarity.
    </p>

    <p>
      Exegetically, I work from the original languages and root my applications in the text before reaching for cultural bridges.
      The culture is never the foundation — it's the bridge. Scripture first. Always.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem;">Background</h2>

    <p>
      I grew up in Texas and have been involved in ministry in various capacities for years before joining Crosspoint staff.
      Outside of ministry and seminary, I'm a husband and father of three young children.
    </p>

  </div>

</Base>
